I had the MP convention sign wrong — empirically MP(c) standardized to mean 1 has κ_r = c^{r-1}. ActB now matches MP perfectly. **And chi_P shows a clear, growing deviation from MP**. Let me extend to multiple drop levels to see if the deviation is bulk-level or finite-rank.
